WEBVTT

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:18.910
<i>They're sho pretty!</i>

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:30.880
Erika Shower!

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:35.570
Stop it, Erika!

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:37.260
Give us a break!

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:39.890
Take that! And that! And that!

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:45.620
Let's all work together and get Erika, everyone!

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:46.810
Right!

00:00:52.570 --> 00:00:53.440
Sawai!

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:53.950
Yes?

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:56.950
Come and help us get Erika, Sawai!

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:03.980
{OP}

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:07.170
HeartCatch

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:08.630
Precure!

00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:12.180
HeartCatch Precure!

00:01:12.230 --> 00:01:15.180
Now, all together

00:01:15.310 --> 00:01:17.680
HeartCatch Precure!

00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:20.690
Let's make our flowers bloom

00:01:25.730 --> 00:01:28.280
Within each of our chests,

00:01:28.450 --> 00:01:30.950
they begin to sprout

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:32.620
The seeds of the heart

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:33.870
are growing

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:36.490
bit by bit

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:37.160
Red,

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:37.790
white

00:01:37.790 --> 00:01:39.080
and yellow

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:41.830
It's because these blooming buds are

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:43.290
all varied colors

00:01:43.630 --> 00:01:44.750
that they

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:46.930
shine so brightly!

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:52.260
That smile that you've nurtured

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:54.760
with such care

00:01:54.890 --> 00:01:57.470
will never wither

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:01.060
HeartCatch Precure!

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:03.940
Now, all together

00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:06.400
HeartCatch Precure!

00:02:06.570 --> 00:02:09.070
Let's make our flowers bloom!

00:02:09.490 --> 00:02:13.990
They're always right by our sides

00:02:13.990 --> 00:02:14.820
So together

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:18.660
let's make those pretty flowers of our heart

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:21.620
bloom even more!

00:02:21.790 --> 00:02:23.120
HeartCatch

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:24.630
Precure!

00:02:33.710 --> 00:02:36.960
I can't think of any new designs...

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:38.420
Me neither...

00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:41.600
We've been drawing pretty much 
non-stop since yesterday, after all...

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:44.470
I can't go on anymore...

00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:46.720
Me neither...

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:48.380
What should we do, President?

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:49.460
Hmm...

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:52.290
To be honest, I'm kinda running out of ideas too...

00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:53.960
I've got it!

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:56.610
Let's go for a walk! It'll be a nice change of pace!

00:02:56.610 --> 00:02:57.630
We can't!

00:02:58.340 --> 00:02:59.500
Why not?

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:02.900
You said you wanted us to light some fireworks together this evening.{I know what you're thinking, this wording is shitty. If you think this wording is shitty, you haven't seen the fireworks it's describing. Any normal description of what fireworks do is completely useless for fireworks as bad as these.}

00:03:02.900 --> 00:03:06.140
You're the one who said we should get the designs done during the day, Erika.

00:03:06.820 --> 00:03:08.670
Right... I did...

00:03:09.710 --> 00:03:12.130
Grr...

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:17.840
It'd be nice if designs would just
 flow through my mind like water...

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:18.880
Oh!

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:22.920
Speaking of water, there's this pond behind the villa.

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:26.010
I think there was a rare flower growing there!

00:03:27.110 --> 00:03:29.760
What was it called, again?

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:32.660
Let's see. It was a water...

00:03:32.660 --> 00:03:33.650
Water ca...

00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:35.900
You mean a water canna?!

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:37.740
Right, that.

00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:39.690
Is it really that rare of a flower?

00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:44.430
It is! It hardly ever grows, and has
 the most beautiful purple flowers...

00:03:48.090 --> 00:03:49.040
Ahem.

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:52.770
W-Well, a little walk couldn't hurt, could it? {Changed We-Well to W-well, as that's how that sort of expression is typically written out in English.}

00:03:52.770 --> 00:03:54.130
All right!

00:03:54.130 --> 00:03:56.290
Yay!

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:02.550
Naomi, what was with that lifeless high five?

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:05.010
I can't wait to see it!

00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:16.440
Be Brave<i>!</i>

00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:16.440
Be Brave<i>!</i>

00:04:27.860 --> 00:04:29.660
The air out here is really nice!

00:04:29.660 --> 00:04:33.290
Yeah, it's really clean and refreshing.{HALP HOW DO I WORD THIS D:}

00:04:33.730 --> 00:04:36.740
A change of pace really is important every now and again, huh?

00:04:36.740 --> 00:04:38.460
Y-Yeah, you're right... {Ye-Yeah to Y-yeah}

00:04:38.860 --> 00:04:42.300
We're nearly there now, so let's keep on moving!

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:45.430
Ahhh, it's a spider!

00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:48.970
Look out!

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:55.810
Sawai, are you all right?

00:04:55.810 --> 00:04:57.520
Y-Yeah...

00:04:59.660 --> 00:05:00.690
Thank goodness.

00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:05.190
Sorry about this.

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:10.000
You'll be all right over here.

00:05:10.920 --> 00:05:12.980
She's so cool!{I THINK, but I'm not sure, that whilst most of them are going "kakkoii" one is going "kawaii" but it's not in the captions. Worth adding in, you think?} {Sure. We'll call it that Aesir special touch. Just don't leave it untranslated.}

00:05:12.980 --> 00:05:14.520
You're so brave, Itsuki!

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:16.950
Will you please walk in front of me?

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:19.990
Sure, fine by me.

00:05:19.990 --> 00:05:21.750
Don't worry! Everything's okay now!

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:24.040
Now let's get back in the adventurous mood and keep walking!

00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:25.300
Okay!

00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:30.010
Naomi?

00:05:30.010 --> 00:05:31.470
Oh, it's nothing. Sorry...

00:05:33.980 --> 00:05:36.160
It feels nice when the water splashes, doesn't it?

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:41.780
Naomi, Itsuki was really cool back there, wasn't she?

00:05:41.780 --> 00:05:42.590
Yeah!

00:05:44.250 --> 00:05:45.110
It's not far, right?

00:05:45.110 --> 00:05:46.450
Just a little further!

00:05:46.450 --> 00:05:51.120
Tsubomi, the thing is, I've always really 
admired the student council president. {This shimmy walk is the GAYEST THING EVER.}

00:05:51.890 --> 00:05:55.250
She's cool, athletic, and great at studying.

00:05:55.830 --> 00:06:00.100
I've always considered her to be special, on a higher level than someone like me.{The Japanese expression for this is awesome. "She always seemed to be above the clouds." which is I guess insinuating out of view and reach etc.} {Very neat! Also, from -> than.}

00:06:00.100 --> 00:06:02.660
I know how you feel, Naomi!

00:06:02.660 --> 00:06:07.500
When I first transferred here, I didn't know Itsuki was a girl,

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:11.290
so I, um... developed a bit of a crush on her...

00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:16.010
We're lucky to have you leading the pack, Itsuki!

00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:19.390
Jeez, Erika, what are you saying?

00:06:19.390 --> 00:06:20.610
Must be nice...

00:06:20.610 --> 00:06:21.580
Naomi?

00:06:21.580 --> 00:06:22.650
Oh, nothing.

00:06:25.370 --> 00:06:30.570
I just don't know what I should do to become friends with the student council president.

00:06:31.900 --> 00:06:36.100
Her joining the same club as me, 
and us all going to camp together...

00:06:36.100 --> 00:06:38.300
I never dreamed something like this would happen.

00:06:39.060 --> 00:06:40.420
Naomi...

00:06:40.870 --> 00:06:45.250
Say... Tsubomi, how did you manage to become friends with the student council president?

00:06:45.540 --> 00:06:47.090
Huh?! Well, um...

00:06:48.020 --> 00:06:51.390
It's kinda hard to explain, really.

00:06:51.890 --> 00:06:53.140
I guess it must be.

00:06:53.890 --> 00:06:58.770
I just wish I could make friends with her as easily as everyone else has. {had -> has}

00:06:59.990 --> 00:07:01.900
But I don't know what I should do.

00:07:08.940 --> 00:07:11.030
It's so beautiful!

00:07:11.030 --> 00:07:12.710
Not bad, Erika!

00:07:13.740 --> 00:07:15.670
It's not bad at all, is it?

00:07:16.880 --> 00:07:18.750
Hey, a water canna! {Of course the pond is heart-shaped.}

00:07:20.750 --> 00:07:22.960
Wow, it's so pretty!

00:07:25.150 --> 00:07:28.670
Well then, I think it's finally time to eat!{"Lunchtime" in English. Which is annoying as the grammar does not take well to random english being shunted in it like that.}

00:07:31.340 --> 00:07:33.550
It looks delicious!

00:07:33.940 --> 00:07:36.770
Your mom's a good cook, Erika!

00:07:36.770 --> 00:07:38.260
She really is!

00:07:38.260 --> 00:07:40.670
These sandwiches are delicious!{YES! YES! THIS IS DELICIOUS!} {Is this sandwich BISOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOON?}

00:07:44.450 --> 00:07:45.230
That was delicious!

00:07:45.230 --> 00:07:48.300
Thanks! I'm sure Mom'll be glad you like 'em!

00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:51.650
Hm?

00:07:51.650 --> 00:07:53.990
Erika, can I have a word?

00:07:54.800 --> 00:07:58.640
I see... So Naomi's worried about that, huh?

00:07:58.640 --> 00:08:03.460
This is as good a chance as she'll get, so it'd be nice if she could become friends with Itsuki...

00:08:03.890 --> 00:08:05.460
What should we do to help her?

00:08:06.160 --> 00:08:08.420
Just leave it to me!

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:12.930
It's time for the Heart-Pounding Whirlwind Seating Arrangement Changing Event!

00:08:12.930 --> 00:08:14.330
Huh?

00:08:16.740 --> 00:08:17.970
E-Erika!

00:08:18.520 --> 00:08:20.930
Um... I-I...

00:08:18.940 --> 00:08:20.930
So, uh... what do we...

00:08:20.930 --> 00:08:24.150
All right, now it's time to start the Exciting Conversation Event!

00:08:24.150 --> 00:08:25.810
Um... err...

00:08:25.810 --> 00:08:28.150
Come on, you two! Get talking, get talking!

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:30.610
Come on, quickly! Quickly!

00:08:29.480 --> 00:08:31.780
E-E-Erika, you idiot!

00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:33.830
Huh?

00:08:33.830 --> 00:08:35.280
Sawai!

00:08:37.340 --> 00:08:40.060
Jeez, Erika, you're so pushy.

00:08:41.040 --> 00:08:42.500
Sorry...

00:08:49.590 --> 00:08:52.280
At last, it is complete!

00:08:52.280 --> 00:08:54.350
My new finisher!

00:08:55.090 --> 00:09:00.100
Big Bang Kumojacky Summer Wave Crasher Special!

00:09:00.820 --> 00:09:02.940
Sasorina! Kobraja!

00:09:02.940 --> 00:09:06.520
Let's show those Precure the results of our training!

00:09:07.300 --> 00:09:08.980
Hm? What's this?

00:09:10.220 --> 00:09:14.810
"Training possesses not a shred of beauty. It doesn't suit me in the slightest.

00:09:14.810 --> 00:09:17.480
But make sure you work hard nonetheless.

00:09:17.480 --> 00:09:18.470
Adieu!"

00:09:18.470 --> 00:09:19.780
What?!

00:09:22.520 --> 00:09:24.820
Oh, so that's where you were, Sasorina?

00:09:25.580 --> 00:09:27.330
Hey. Sasorina!

00:09:29.080 --> 00:09:31.210
Why are you spacing out like that?

00:09:31.900 --> 00:09:33.090
Wait, I remember!

00:09:44.700 --> 00:09:46.720
So that's why?

00:09:46.720 --> 00:09:48.560
Hmph! Well, that's fine.

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:51.440
I shall walk this path alone!

00:09:51.440 --> 00:09:53.800
That's what being a man is all about!

00:09:53.800 --> 00:09:55.650
Say your prayers, Precure!

00:10:15.050 --> 00:10:17.270
I'm such a wimp, aren't I?

00:10:18.430 --> 00:10:21.760
Erika gave me the perfect opportunity, and I just...

00:10:25.250 --> 00:10:27.790
It seems I've found a sad little runt!{He's parodying Sasorina's "I've found a sad little girl!" near verbatim, but replacing the 'ko' (child) with 'yatsu'. The "it seems" is just flavor text on my part to match his more knightly tone and ZE YO}

00:10:29.040 --> 00:10:29.770
Who are you?!

00:10:31.650 --> 00:10:35.610
The Flower of your Heart has withered, so I shall take it!

00:10:36.310 --> 00:10:39.610
Flower of the Heart, show yourself!

00:10:49.740 --> 00:10:53.190
You're up, Desertrian!

00:10:58.480 --> 00:10:59.050
What?

00:10:59.480 --> 00:11:00.670
A Desertrian!

00:11:02.470 --> 00:11:05.100
Green teaaaa!

00:11:17.480 --> 00:11:19.150
Ichuki!

00:11:19.150 --> 00:11:20.230
Potpourri?!

00:11:21.530 --> 00:11:24.370
We have to shtop the Desertrian before it comes any closher!

00:11:24.370 --> 00:11:25.040
Right!

00:11:35.020 --> 00:11:38.170
Sheed of the Precure, go forth!

00:11:41.130 --> 00:11:42.310
Precure!

00:11:42.310 --> 00:11:43.720
Open My Heart!

00:12:24.460 --> 00:12:27.300
A lone flower, bathing in the Sun's rays!

00:12:30.270 --> 00:12:31.970
Cure Sunshine!

00:12:37.730 --> 00:12:39.840
Green tea!

00:12:52.680 --> 00:12:56.210
So the third Precure makes her entrance, huh?

00:12:56.660 --> 00:12:57.750
Go get her!

00:13:11.140 --> 00:13:14.810
This third Precure isn't bad at all!

00:13:26.600 --> 00:13:27.580
Did we keep you waiting?

00:13:27.580 --> 00:13:29.240
We're sorry for being so late!

00:13:29.240 --> 00:13:30.740
Blossom? Marine?!

00:13:32.230 --> 00:13:34.330
All right, this is where the battle really begins!

00:13:34.670 --> 00:13:36.990
So you two finally bothered to show up.

00:13:36.990 --> 00:13:40.340
Desertrian! Crush them into dust!

00:13:40.340 --> 00:13:42.460
Green tea tea tea tea!

00:13:45.380 --> 00:13:47.590
Greeeeeeen teeaaaaaa!

00:13:55.680 --> 00:14:01.300
I just want to be friends with 
the student council president! {This is fucking lame.}

00:14:01.300 --> 00:14:03.890
I just want to be friends!

00:14:04.490 --> 00:14:08.110
But I'm just too nervous to be able to talk to her!

00:14:08.540 --> 00:14:11.160
I can't even make eye contact with her!

00:14:11.490 --> 00:14:16.810
Why is it when I look at her face, I can never find the words I want to say?!

00:14:16.810 --> 00:14:20.670
I just want to make friends with her like everyone else has!

00:14:23.090 --> 00:14:24.550
Blossom! Marine!

00:14:34.310 --> 00:14:36.480
The student council president!

00:14:44.070 --> 00:14:48.520
I just want to be friends with 
the student council president!

00:14:48.520 --> 00:14:50.860
I want to be her friend!

00:14:51.360 --> 00:14:53.290
Just how should I...

00:14:54.220 --> 00:14:55.770
respond to Naomi's feelings? {SHUT UP AND STOP SAYING THE SAME THING OVER AND OVER AGAIN perhaps.}

00:14:55.770 --> 00:14:57.240
How ridiculous.

00:14:58.030 --> 00:15:00.230
You want to be friends?

00:15:00.230 --> 00:15:04.710
Such a ludicrous reason for the 
Flower of your Heart to wither so.

00:15:04.710 --> 00:15:07.460
There is but one way to make a true friend!

00:15:07.460 --> 00:15:10.340
And that is to let your burning fists do the talking! {Kumojacky almost saves this episode.}

00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:14.010
So cease your whining and plunge headlong at her!

00:15:14.010 --> 00:15:15.760
Get her, Desertrian!

00:15:15.760 --> 00:15:18.060
Green tea!

00:15:25.470 --> 00:15:29.070
She may not know how she should become friends with the girl she most admires,

00:15:29.070 --> 00:15:32.660
but that doesn't mean you can just
 ridicule the pain a girl feels in her heart!

00:15:32.660 --> 00:15:36.620
Using her heart to create a 
Desertrian like that is just cruel!

00:15:36.620 --> 00:15:39.160
I just want us to be friends!

00:15:39.510 --> 00:15:42.130
Making friends is really simple, you know!

00:15:42.130 --> 00:15:45.630
You already want to be friends with her, after all!

00:15:47.440 --> 00:15:49.280
Marine's right!

00:15:49.280 --> 00:15:53.730
If you both feel that way, then you 
and Itsuki are already friends, Naomi!

00:15:53.730 --> 00:15:55.220
Right, Sunshine?

00:15:55.220 --> 00:15:56.100
Yeah!

00:15:56.440 --> 00:15:57.560
We're friends!

00:15:58.200 --> 00:16:00.770
You and I are already friends!

00:16:02.000 --> 00:16:04.860
I-I'm so happy!

00:16:05.180 --> 00:16:06.630
Desertrian!

00:16:06.630 --> 00:16:11.650
You cannot become stronger with such a half-hearted attempt at friendship!

00:16:11.950 --> 00:16:13.030
Kumojacky!

00:16:13.030 --> 00:16:14.200
Hm?

00:16:14.490 --> 00:16:16.990
Everyone has their own ideal of what friendship means to them!

00:16:16.990 --> 00:16:21.200
But you force your beliefs on others and
 belittle those who think differently from you.

00:16:21.920 --> 00:16:26.880
That darkness in your heart... 
shall be illuminated by my light!

00:16:36.280 --> 00:16:39.270
Gather, Floral Power!

00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:43.510
Shiny Tambourine!

00:16:57.780 --> 00:16:59.830
Flowers, dance for me!

00:17:00.440 --> 00:17:06.640
Precure Gold Forte Burst!

00:17:26.810 --> 00:17:30.010
Tch... But this is where the real fight begins!

00:17:30.010 --> 00:17:32.650
Behold, my new finisher!

00:17:32.650 --> 00:17:38.820
Big Bang Kumojacky Summer Wave Crasher Special!

00:17:49.990 --> 00:17:53.170
Gather, Floral Power!

00:17:54.600 --> 00:17:56.800
Blossom Tact!

00:18:05.830 --> 00:18:07.390
Flowers, shine forth!

00:18:10.920 --> 00:18:15.180
Precure Pink Forte Wave!

00:18:23.450 --> 00:18:24.410
What?!

00:18:33.930 --> 00:18:35.630
Flowers, glitter bright!

00:18:39.000 --> 00:18:44.050
Precure Blue Forte Wave!

00:18:47.600 --> 00:18:48.280
Tch...

00:18:55.230 --> 00:18:56.390
Hmph.

00:18:56.390 --> 00:18:58.840
You've gotten stronger, haven't you?

00:18:58.840 --> 00:19:01.960
All the better to keep me entertained.{He's literally just saying "This is getting more and more fun." Feel free to slap me back into place if you like. :w} {He doesn't look like he's having fun. This line can stand.}

00:19:16.960 --> 00:19:19.600
If we have this many to choose from, everything should go perfectly!

00:19:19.600 --> 00:19:23.220
So I think that wraps up our 
designing for the school festival!

00:19:25.500 --> 00:19:28.180
Right then, it's finally time to play with some fireworks!

00:19:28.180 --> 00:19:30.240
Let's hurry and change into our yukata!

00:19:30.240 --> 00:19:32.150
Right!

00:19:34.480 --> 00:19:36.570
Thank goodness you've finally woken up.{"come back around" -> "woken up"}

00:19:37.480 --> 00:19:38.780
President!

00:19:39.150 --> 00:19:41.380
We found you lying unconscious in the woods. {I may or may not have touched you inappropriately.}

00:19:42.200 --> 00:19:43.240
Are you all right?

00:19:43.940 --> 00:19:45.760
You did?

00:19:45.760 --> 00:19:48.280
How strange. Did I not get enough sleep or something?

00:19:48.280 --> 00:19:49.960
Don't worry, though. I'm all right now.

00:19:50.410 --> 00:19:51.830
That's good.

00:19:51.830 --> 00:19:55.000
Looks like you'll be able to enjoy the fireworks with us, Naomi.{Apart from the group as a whole, no subject is specified in this sentence. If you like, feel free to change this to "we'll be able to enjoy the fireworks with the others" if you want to imply Itsuki would forego them in favour of caring for her new strumpet.} {Meh. Nah.}

00:19:56.960 --> 00:20:00.040
Well then, I'll help you change into your yukata.

00:20:00.040 --> 00:20:00.920
Thanks.

00:20:05.780 --> 00:20:06.850
